# exits.psv -- how to leave a program that does not finish on its own.
# name | the way out, in the card's own style: keys in `backquotes'.
#
# The card shows this on a line of its own, highlighted, right under "Try it":
# the lifejacket that makes it safe to just try something.  Every line was
# confirmed by leaving the program that way under the emulator, not assumed.
accordian|`x', then `n' at `Play again?'
advent|`quit' Return, then `y' Return
advint|`quit' Return, then `y' Return
animal|`Control-C'
arithmetic|`Control-C'
atc|`Control-C', then `y'
back|`Control-C'
backgammon|`q' Return, then `y' Return
bandit|`q' Return at the bet prompt
bjack|`0' Return at `Wager?'
blackjack|`0' Return at `Wager?', then `n' Return
blackjak|`Control-C'
bks|`q', then `q' again at the menu
bog|`Control-C'
bs|no key leaves mid-game: play it out, then `n' at `[yn]?'
bugs|`q'
c4|`q'
canfield|`q' Return, then `n' Return
castle|`q' then `y'
chess|`Control-E'
convert|`quit' Return, then `y' Return
corewar|any key at `Hit any key to continue'
craps|`q'
crib|`Control-C'
cribbage|`Control-C'
drawpoker|`F' then `y'
fish|`quit' Return
fuddle|`Control-C'
gnuchess|`quit' Return
gnuchessc|`quit' Return
gnuchessn|`quit' Return
gnuchessr|`quit' Return
gnugo|`stop' Return, then `n' Return
hack|`Q' then `y'
hang|`Control-C'
hexa|`q'
hinterhalt|`Control-C'
hotel|`Q' then `y'
infocom|`quit' Return, then `y' Return -- Space first at any `[MORE]'
infocom.tcap|`quit' Return, then `y' Return
jotto|`Control-C'
jumble2|`q' Return, then `q' Return again
kalah|`-1' Return twice, then `q' Return
knight|`q'
lander|`q' at the title; in flight, land or crash, then `n' and Space
larn|`Q' then `y'
letters|stop typing: the words reach the bottom and the game ends
mastrm|`Control-C'
mille|`q' then `y'
mines|`q'
monop|`quit' Return, then `yes' Return
moria|`Control-K', `Q', then any key twice
mw|`Q'
mz|`Control-C'
napoleon|`quit' Return, then `q' Return
nchess|`quit' Return
nethack3|`Q', `y', then `n'
nobs|`Control-C'
othello|`Q'
pacman|`q'
paranoia|`Control-C'
perp|`Control-C'
poker|`Control-C'
reversi|`Control-E'
robots|`Control-C'
rogue|`Q' then `y', then Space twice
saa|`q', then `n'
scrabble|`Q', `y', then `n'
shuffle|`q'
ski|`Control-C'
snake|`x'
sod|`q', then Return
sokoban|`q'
sol|`q' Return
solx|`q' Return
stone|`Control-C'
teachgammon|`Control-C'
tess|`quit' Return, then `n' Return
tet|`q', then `q' again at the menu
thricken|`q'
torus|`q'
trek|`terminate' Return, then `n' Return
trek73|`Control-C', then `yes' Return
tt|`q'
tttt|`q'
typefast|`Control-C'
ularn|`Q' then `y'
vcraps|`X'
wanderer|`q'
world|`quit' Return, then `y' Return
worm|`Control-C'
wump|`q' Return
yahtzee|`q'
yahtzee2|`q' then `y'
yidslots|`0' Return
bio|`Control-C'
biory|Return at `Name Vorname'
bite|`q'
cam|`Control-C'
card|`Control-C'
checkfile|`Q'
chemtab|`6' on the main menu
cvtbase|`Escape'
dc|`Q'
help|`q', then Return twice
juggle|`Control-C'
less|`q'
life|`Control-C'
loan|`Control-C'
logisim|`Escape' then `y'
lotto|`Control-C'
man|`q'
more|`q' then Return
mwb|`j' down to `Exit session', then Return
oleo|`Escape' `x', then `kill-oleo' and Return
rain|`Control-C'
rot22|`Control-C'
rpn|`q' then Return
sc|`q' then `y'
scqref|`q'
textb|`Control-C'
vc|`Control-C'
worms|`Control-C'
wysecrack|`Control-C', once its first line is out a minute in
xmas|`Control-C'
adldebug|`q' and Return
adlrun|`quit' and Return
beav|`Control-C', then `y' and Return, leaving without saving
ed|`Q' and Return, leaving without writing
editor|`!'
elvis|`Escape', then `:q!' and Return, leaving without saving
elvis_input|`Escape', then `:q!' and Return, leaving without saving
em|`Control-X' `Control-C', then `y' if it asks about changes
emacs|`Control-X' `Control-C', then `y' if it asks about changes
forth|`bye' and Return
gshell|`!'
hexedit|`q'
hist|`logout' and Return
me|`Control-X' `Control-C', then `j' if it asks about changes
mg|`Control-X' `Control-C', then `n' and `yes' Return if it asks about changes
mshell|`Control-C'
sh|`exit' and Return
stevie|`Escape', then `:q!' and Return, leaving without saving
umacs|`Control-X' `Control-C', then `y' if it asks about changes
vi|`Escape', then `:q!' and Return, leaving without saving
vi.elvis|`Escape', then `:q!' and Return, leaving without saving
vi_1.0|`Escape', then `:q!' and Return, leaving without saving
view|`Escape', then `:q!' and Return, leaving without saving
wam.sbprolog|`halt.' and Return
wish|`Control-D'
xlisp|`(exit)' and Return
bc|`quit' then Return
